       Q: Is there a minimum acceptable production output (e.g. ≥ 80% of the baseline shift volume) below which a high efficiency ratio would still be unacceptable — because without a floor the optimiser could maximise efficiency by running at near-idle pace and still satisfy all hard constraints?
