       Q: Does the 80 dB limit apply as (a) a continuous instantaneous ceiling at every moment, (b) a 1-hour rolling LAeq, or (c) the full 8-hour shift LAeq — because treating it as an 8-hour average would allow the optimiser to schedule loud operations in early hours while staying within the average, exposing operators to transient peaks well above 80 dB?
